    {"type":"txt", "css":"ptf-section-title", "data":"- Implications"},
    {"type":"txt:ol", "data":[
      "<b>T</b>he <b>3D</b> model has been fully remade from scratch, as the original (from <b>2007</b>) was a single-mesh-mess, too far from nowadays' standards.",
      "<b>T</b>extures are made from scrath too, taking originals as a mere reference.",
      "<b-0>JBEAM</b> syntax is a custom <b-0>JSON</b> derivation so the base is the same, it's used to define and setup the actual vehicle physic structures, lights, variables and other behaviours.",
      "<b-0>LUA</b> is the main language for most of the game engine content, it's used to drive the extra logic added to this specific vehicle such as the radar and some engine behaviours.",
      "<b-0>Javascript</b>, <b-0>HTML</b> and <b-0>CSS</b> are the languages for all UI and <b>2D</b> rendering via <b-0>Angular Components</b>, it's used to make the radar's <b-0>LUA</b> frontend to use it as a <b>2D</b> texture."
    ]},
